{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1157085-mouse-in-the-new-age","id":1157085,"title":"Mouse in the new age","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-08T12:11:37-08:00","id":1157085,"title":"Mouse in the new age","content":"Has anyone else noticed how much mice are responsible for a lot of modern medicine and tech? We use them for the vast majority of animal trials and in doing so labs that use mice for testing construct massive &quot;Play Areas&quot; where mice are well fed, given a number of toys to play with, and are allowed to roam around a web of play pins with other mice. There are even many people in the science communities that practically revere them.<br /> <br /> Thinking all of this, is it possible that an aspect of Mouse could rise as a powerful weaver totem? How would the garou react to that? What would said totem be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T14:01:48-08:00","id":1157118,"title":"","content":"I think that Mouse still has more than enough of an unregulated base to continue on not under the sway of the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T15:00:27-08:00","id":1157132,"title":"","content":"I think a problem is that these are not things that mice are doing, but are things being done to mice. This is a lot different than creatures whose actual behavior seem to embody or typify certain qualities such as Ants, Bees, and Beavers. They would embody certain aspects of the Weaver since they alter their environment, and humans consider them to be &quot;industrious&quot; or &quot;hard working&quot; or represent social differentiation. Cockroach is a totem of the Glass Walkers because it embodies traits of an animal that is able to thrive among human societies and the largest cities, and these traits would be useful to a Garou who wish to do the same. What would be the traits of a lab mouse? That it is experimented upon, a creature forced by others. Perhaps eventually it might become associated with a brood of specific Weaver spirits, but probably never a powerful totem.<br /> <br /> Even if you go this route, it may simply mean a differentiation between Mouse and say Laboratory Mouse as two different spirits. After all, lab mice are specifically bred to be different than the mice species in the wild. Lab mice are simply a variant of house mice, and there are lots of different kinds of mice out there without any kind of the same affiliation as the lab mouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T17:22:36-08:00","id":1157158,"title":"","content":"This is something that has happened in a past game I participated in, we discovered Laboratory Mouse as a totem. It wasn't strong but it had interest in us, the pack was comprised of mostly Metis and it saw part of its nature in us. It didnt offer us gifts in return for our services, it gave us Hedge Magic Alchemy/Chemistry ranks and a boost of intelligence . We were only required to complete complex puzzles, never interfere in the pursuit of sciences. This got us in some trouble, but the local Glasswalkers tried to get the spirit into their territory because it wasnt completely a Weaver spirit, it had its own goals and abilities. <br /> <br /> There is a question of how easily would the Lab Mouse fall to the Wyrm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T18:40:20-08:00","id":1157165,"title":"","content":"As another model organism, rats nonetheless don't see Rat falling to the Weaver but rather going apeshit as The Rat God, which is more like falling to the Wyld. Even the Weaver-ish Engineer Ratkin Freaks are still on the crazy side. As such, I don't know that Mouse's reaction would be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T06:09:38-08:00","id":1157260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1157085-mouse-in-the-new-age?p=1157132#post1157132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a problem is that these are not things that mice are doing, but are things being done to mice. This is a lot different than creatures whose actual behavior seem to embody or typify certain qualities such as Ants, Bees, and Beavers. They would embody certain aspects of the Weaver since they alter their environment, and humans consider them to be &quot;industrious&quot; or &quot;hard working&quot; or represent social differentiation. Cockroach is a totem of the Glass Walkers because it embodies traits of an animal that is able to thrive among human societies and the largest cities, and these traits would be useful to a Garou who wish to do the same. What would be the traits of a lab mouse? That it is experimented upon, a creature forced by others. Perhaps eventually it might become associated with a brood of specific Weaver spirits, but probably never a powerful totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I though that was the point though, that a totem forms around what an animal represents rather than what it does. Like how gryphons don't run around in the wild, but represent un restrained nature as a totem just the same.<br /> <br /> I was thinking Lab Mouse would be like a portion of mouse that began to represent sacrifice for a greater cause and the fact that this representation was spreading as scientific investigation of medicine increased. That's also why I think i'd be powerful, because it'd have a sort of renown amoung all the places that the weaver is strongest, and thus be known to weaver spirits and scientists a-like<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1157085-mouse-in-the-new-age?p=1157165#post1157165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another model organism, rats nonetheless don't see Rat falling to the Weaver but rather going apeshit as The Rat God, which is more like falling to the Wyld. Even the Weaver-ish Engineer Ratkin Freaks are still on the crazy side. As such, I don't know that Mouse's reaction would be different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mice and rats are two completely different animals, though, I don't know how much that affects the spirits that are representations of those animals. It would be somewhat poetic though if the spirits of mouse and rat found themselves like brothers on different sides of a war between the weaver and the wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T11:41:43-08:00","id":1157321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1157085-mouse-in-the-new-age?p=1157260#post1157260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mice and rats are two completely different animals, though, I don't know how much that affects the spirits that are representations of those animals. It would be somewhat poetic though if the spirits of mouse and rat found themselves like brothers on different sides of a war between the weaver and the wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're two envelopes of whole messes of different animals where one particular species of each happens to be an extensively-used model organism in biological studies. Nonetheless, Rat does not appear to have an aspect expressing this as something that the spirit endorses, and I can't find a reason for Mouse to, either, since they're also going to be thriving in the cracks of humanity's edifices when not used as model organisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}